"notes 
" nested structure is a structure where we have  a 
"internal structure that means structure inside there is structure 
"when it comes to memory allocation that structure follow the same one by one memory allocation 
"but when it comes to nested structure it make a  whole structure in place of 1 field inside it it allocate the structure then follow to nest fields 
 TO understand the flow lets take the xample of the file directory 

EG: a employee folder have employee deatils inside there is one more folder that have the 
employement deatils like dept , designation 
EG--- employee
       ---- ename , empno (these are the fields)
       ----- dept (inner structure )
               |
               |----- deptno , dname.( these are the nested structure )
         ------empdesign ( this is again afield in outer structure )
       end of employee structure.(outer structure).

"code #########


report  znested_structure.

 data : begin of emp, "outer structure 
        empno type i,
        ename (20) type c,
                 
         begin of dept,"inner structure 
           deptno type i, 
          dname(20) type c ,
          end of dept,
        empdesig(20) type c , 
end of emp.



emp~empno = 1.
emp~ename = 'raju'.
emp~dept~deptno = 10.
emp~dept~dname = 'sales'.
emp~empdesig = 'manager'.

Write :/ (20) 'Employee no : ', emp~empno,
      / (20) 'Employee name : ', emp~ename,
      /(20) 'Employee dept : ', emp~dept~deptno,
       / (20) 'Employee  dept name  : ', emp~dept~dname,
        /(20) 'designation  : ', emp~empdesign,




